[2025-11-22T15:21:27] codex

Completed extraction per DE_Guide_v10_1.md and populated the JSON.

What I did
- Parsed Han2024B.pdf.md and S0033291724002617sup001.docx.md for all required items.
- Extracted dataset names, Ns, demographics, modality, analysis level, preprocessing, QC, site harmonization.
- Captured normative modeling details (GPR, predictors, response, validation strategies).
- Summarized clinical datasets, deviation metrics, association analyses, key findings, and limitations.
- Added precise supporting quotes with locations (file + line ranges/sections).

Output file updated
- DE_Han2024B_by_codex_20251123001816.json

Highlights
- Datasets: DIDA-MDD; REST-meta-MDD.
- HCs: 1079 (DIDA-MDD); 1104 (REST-meta-MDD); Total 2183.
- Modality: Resting-state fMRI (ALFF), ROI-level (brain connectome atlas; 246 regions).
- Preprocessing: DPARSF v5.4, standard steps with scrubbing (discovery); DARTEL normalization (validation).
- QC: Rigorous QC noted; scrubbing; analyses controlled for mean FD.
- Site handling: ComBat per dataset.
- Normative model: New; Gaussian process regression with age and sex.
- Validation: 10-fold CV (100x), leave-one-site-out, cross-dataset generalization, alternate atlas; “Partial” for nuisance handling adequacy.
- Deviation metric: Z-scores; |Z|>2.6 used for extreme deviation analysis.
- Findings: Four differential factors linking to clinical features, neurotransmitter maps, inflammation-related genes, and network epicenters; replication across datasets.
- Limitations: Clinical detail/comorbidity limitations, no medication dose/type quantification, cross-sectional design.

If you’d like, I can also generate a brief CSV summary or verify any specific field against the source text again.
